      "title": "DNA double helix",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "Twenty base pairs of B-DNA, about 100 million times life size: 10 pairs per turn, 2 nm wide, with the major and minor grooves. Bases: A green, T red, G yellow, C blue. A-T pairs share two hydrogen bonds, G-C pairs three. Separate unzips the two strands."
        },
